  "term": "pseudoephedrine",
  "definition": "Pseudoephedrine is a phenethylamine related to ephedrine that acts on the sympathetic nervous system. It increases norepinephrine release and has weak direct effects at alpha- and beta-adrenergic receptors, leading to blood vessel narrowing and reduced nasal and sinus congestion.",
